  "id": "arthrogryposis-multiplex-congenita",
  "term": "arthrogryposis multiplex congenita",
  "definition": "Arthrogryposis multiplex congenita is a congenital, non-progressive motor disorder marked by joint contractures and varying limb movement limitations, often without central nervous system involvement. In psychology and assessment contexts, it is used as a condition for examining how restricted movement—especially impaired hand use—may affect children’s cognitive development and intelligence test performance.",
